  "protocol": "P2-gray-sharpening-overlay-native-representation-check-v1",
  "protocolBoundaries": {
    "candidate": "Instrumented copy of PreviewCanonicalHalfFIT's production writer, 256-row RGBA32F native bands, exact four-component finite checks, normalized hardware 2x linear sample. Every completed half texel is compared, and the original materializer consumes it.",
    "floatDifferences": "Counts differing 32-bit component representations, not Hamming bit counts. Coordinates in raw half-texture storage. SHA excludes Metal row padding.",
    "limits": "One Apple GPU / OS. Additional radius-1 threshold combinations have not been tested. Other plan topologies were challenged deliberately; differences cannot demonstrate failure for the one passing parameter set.",
    "natural": "One whole-extent scale(0.5) evaluation into an unflipped private RGBA32F texture with the same original CIContext, linear extended sRGB, premultiplied alpha and 512 MiB target. Only the joined output is streamed to disk for comparison.",
    "plan": "Historical 512 MiB display signature is 19 or 21 planned passes, 10*W+108 overdraw and 3*N+N/4+2*2400*1600+20*W+144 processed pixels. RGB is independently excluded by recipe semantics.",
    "realEntry": "Unmodified DevelopmentRendererV3.develop with genuine FlashRaw GPU decode and pin, followed by unmodified V3PreviewMaterializer and copyDisplayRGBA8.",
    "timing": "Correctness workload with two materializations, streamed complete reference storage, comparisons, hashes and public estimates. Peak is process-wide diagnostic footprint. No isolated latency comparison, no ABBA, no claim on speed."
  },
  "reason": [
    "Only one archived gray parameter set per real RAW passes both independent comparisons. Its public plan totals also match the RGB sharpening negative control.",
    "An explicit radius of 3 preserves the displayed bytes but changes some native half-plane RGB values on both RAWs.",
    "The radius-1.75 / sparse-edges case changes both native half bits and displayed bytes on both RAWs.",
    "On independent finite half-float HDR data at 5100x3400, both explicit halfs match bitwise yet both displays differ from the original whole FIT."
  ],
